<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">mana</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">mana</ansi> (Magic/MP) stat represents how much magic you can channel.
Every spell costs mana. Mana does not come back on its own, in a fight or
out of one, for you or your companions. It returns only through:

  a finished camp rest (<ansi fg="command">help camp</ansi>), which fills it for the company;
  a finished night at an inn (<ansi fg="command">help inn</ansi>), which does the same;
  a mana draught (<ansi fg="command">help draughts</ansi>), 25%, 40% or 60% of your mana at once;
  half the mana of a chant a blow breaks (<ansi fg="command">help interrupts</ansi>);
  coming back from death, which leaves you with half (<ansi fg="command">help resurrect</ansi>).

Gaining a level raises your maximum but doesn't refill what you have.

Wizards, witches, shamans and clerics have deep pools: a wizard has 40 mana plus 10 a level,
a witch the same, a cleric 36 plus 9 a level. Everyone else has 4 plus 1 a level. Every
point of Mysticism adds 3 more. In a battle, healers and casters
spend it on their own (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>), and after one your healers
patch the company up with what they have left (<ansi fg="command">help patch</ansi>). An item's
mana recovery bonus helps only enemies now.

Mana will change color to reflect how much you have left:

